# Performance Rules (src/)

Optimize only when justified. Never sacrifice API clarity for micro-optimizations.

## Hot paths to watch

- Visual tree depth and repeated traversal (`GetVisualDescendants` in loops)
- Binding count per control and per list item
- Allocations in layout/render (LINQ, closures, boxing)
- Event subscriptions without cleanup

## Bindings

- Prefer compiled bindings in AXAML consumers
- Minimize bindings in item templates (lists, grids)
- Converters must be stateless and lightweight

## Collections

- Prefer virtualization for long lists
- No per-item services or subscriptions without cleanup
- Cache template parts in `OnApplyTemplate` — resolve once

## Attached properties

Lightweight setters only — no heavy computation on change.

## Lifecycle

No heavy work in `OnApplyTemplate`, `OnAttachedToVisualTree` that runs repeatedly.
